      "content": "The pressure of those expectations is suffocating, and the public perception feels like a spotlight on your failure. If the descent is unbearable, it's time to stop the fall, not by trying to patch up the wreckage, but by taking a deliberate step away from the performance. Reaching out to a crisis line or a therapist can provide immediate, confidential support when the weight of shame becomes too much to carry alone.",
      "source": "target",
